In this context, treasury shares may also be acquired using put or call options or forward contracts, or a combination of these instruments (derivatives).Derivatives may be issued or acquired, excluding any subscription right of the shareholders, with a credit or financial institution, or another appropriate contractual party that is experienced in the derivatives business, with the proviso that, on the basis of the derivatives, only shares will be delivered that were acquired in keeping with the principle of equal treatment.Moreover, the issuance or acquisition of derivatives may be publicly offered to all shareholders or may be effected through the derivatives exchange 
Eurex or a comparable successor system after prior announcement in the Company's designated publication media, with the exclusion of any subscription rights.
